## Hand-authored chunk patterns in a compact text DSL.
##
## One pattern per line:   id ; difficulty ; min-max ; weight ; tags ; row0 row1 ... row9
## Each row is three characters (left, centre, right lane). Row 0 is reached first.
##
## Legend
##   .  empty                 c  coins (ground line)        a  coin arc (jump for fun)
##   >  coins drifting right  <  coins drifting left
##   T  train (roof walkable) t  train + coins on the roof  M  moving train (oncoming)
##   l  low barrier (jump)    J  low barrier + coin arc
##   h  high barrier (roll)   u  high barrier + coins underneath
##   X  full barrier (dodge)  R  ramp up to a train roof
##   G  gap (jump)            g  gap + coin arc
##   P  power-up slot         B  mystery box                d  hazard light (decor telegraph)
##
## Authoring rules: keep the 5 rows in front of an M train empty in its lane (it sweeps them);
## put R directly in front of T/t cells; every pattern is re-checked by the solvability
## validator at load (max difficulty is lowered automatically if it stops being solvable).
class_name PatternData
extends RefCounted

